WEBVTT

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:06.770
Push!

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.490
Backs! I can't hear you!

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:21.250
I'm going to die.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.200
The captain's full of energy today.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.020
Did something happen to him?

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.630
Hey, you! Take this seriously!

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.380
Oh, sorry.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.140
What was that?

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:39.030
<b>Episode 15 
Teammate</b>

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.260
I'm exhausted.

00:02:36.630 --> 00:02:38.880
I'm not done yet!

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.820
I still want to practice.

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:43.890
I can't wait for the training camp.

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:45.970
Gion-kun, you have too much energy.

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.730
I want to be a flanker now.

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:51.480
A flanker...

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.120
Flanker, flanker, flanker!

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:55.380
Shut up!

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.100
Hey, Oharano.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.570
How do I become a flanker?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.450
What? I don't know.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.410
You're the one who told me to be one!

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.650
I didn't say that.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:09.460
You did! At the beach!

00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:11.780
Take responsibility for your words
and tell me what to do!

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:12.580
You're so annoying.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:16.320
You two went to the beach together?

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:18.670
I didn't realize you were so close.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.970
Why would I go to the beach with this guy?

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:26.970
He's talking about when Coach 
took us to the beach to dig holes.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.500
Kitamachi, what are you looking at?

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:32.780
The coach's blog.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.100
Again?

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:39.070
Wow, the old man's been 
eating some tasty stuff.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:41.480
I'm hungry.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:42.450
<b>X Day Before 
Summer Vacation</b>

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.300
"X Day"? What does that mean?

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.020
Maybe it's a day dedicated 
to eating good food.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:50.580
Does that mean he'll be eating 
good food over summer break?

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.450
Let's make him take us with him!

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:53.080
When is it?

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:57.350
If that day's sometime in summer break,
 maybe it'll be during the training camp.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:01.600
Is the food good in Sugadaira, too?

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:02.520
...Sir?

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.760
Huh? Yeah.

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.350
There's a good crêpe shop there.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:09.490
Crêpes?

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:11.370
The captain likes crêpes?

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:15.290
Hurry up and go home.

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.230
Good work today!

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.740
Ise, you're not coming?

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:26.010
Oh, nah. You go on ahead.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.190
Good work today, guys.

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.310
See you later.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:32.770
Later, Ise.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:06.200
Natsuki.

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.230
Shall we go?

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:21.460
<b>Ise</b>

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:21.050
Come in.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:23.210
Excuse the intrusion.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:26.340
Sorry. The place is a mess.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:27.720
It's fine.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:43.570
It's been a year already, huh?

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:52.870
You talked to your brother yesterday 
about the training camp, right?

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:00.990
What?

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.590
Natsuki, is someone else here?

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:06.840
What?

00:06:07.490 --> 00:06:08.850
Excuse the intrusion.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:11.970
Um, I'm Natsuki-kun's teammate—

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:15.130
Why haven't you offered 
your guest anything, idiot?

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:15.790
Hey!

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.060
Don't worry about me.

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:21.110
Oh, sorry. He's just an idiot.

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:26.060
You're the guy who came last year, aren't you?

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:28.450
What was your name again?

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:32.090
Well, whatever. I'll just call you Piggy.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:34.830
Mutsumi-san.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:35.660
What?

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:37.770
Mutsumi-san!

00:06:37.770 --> 00:06:40.420
What was that, huh?

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:40.420
Natsuki, it's okay.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.250
Oh, um... I just...

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:43.170
Hello?

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.980
Oh, yes. Thank you for earlier.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:50.050
No, no. It was fine.

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:49.810
Sorry.

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:51.640
It's fine.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:51.640
Thank you, thank you.

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:20.600
Yesterday, Natsuki told me that 
your team's going to a training camp.

00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:24.360
Ise Natsuki can't go.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:27.420
Um—

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:32.060
I let him go last year because
you were so persistent,

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:34.220
but I told you at the time...

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:36.720
Our parents are dead.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:39.760
They were in an accident six years ago.

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:42.430
I was 20, and Natsuki was 10.

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:44.770
I've put him through 
middle school and high school.

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:50.360
Listen, we just don't have the money.

00:07:50.890 --> 00:07:54.700
How long are you going to
keep messing around in clubs?

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:58.140
You should start working already, loser.

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:03.210
I'm the one who forced him to join.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:07.090
Why would you do that?

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.630
Because I thought playing rugby with him...

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:21.940
...would be fun.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:29.020
I was right.

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:32.930
He's always straightforward
 and hardworking.

00:08:35.730 --> 00:08:37.260
He smiles all the time.

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:41.730
I'm glad I recruited him.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.070
...ease.

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:57.660
Please!

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:07.230
I... I know I'm not doing the right thing.

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:12.730
I'm really grateful to you.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:18.240
But...

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:22.620
I want to go to the training camp.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.010
I want to play rugby.

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:29.090
Please!

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:31.250
Natsuki.

00:09:37.060 --> 00:09:39.680
What's this? Are you two a couple?

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.460
A lot of your <i>persuasion</i>
 play rugby, don't they?

00:09:48.840 --> 00:09:50.600
I see now.

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:52.900
You could've just said
you don't want to be apart—

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:57.200
You piece of shit.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:58.700
You piece of shit!

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:01.700
You don't know anything!

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:04.700
You bastard, Natsuki.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:09.180
Mutsumi-san, you have to leave!

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:10.710
Hey, wait!

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:11.730
Natsuki!

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:13.340
Please leave!

00:10:14.520 --> 00:10:16.720
I'm quitting the team!

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:18.550
I quit!

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:19.220
Natsuki!

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.500
Tell him I can't afford it.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:23.470
Wai—

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.510
Tell the captain I'm sorry.

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:29.030
Mutsumi-san, thanks for everything.

00:10:29.030 --> 00:10:30.650
Natsuki, I'll come back tomorrow—

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:31.950
It's fine.

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:33.900
Thank you.

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:38.030
<b>Ise</b>

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:46.060
<b>Natsuki-kun is popular with the Hachioji Family</b>

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:46.060
<b>Nat-chan, 
let's play 
games</b>

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:46.060
<b>Nat-chan, 
Nat-chan, 
let's play 
hide and 
seek</b>

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:46.060
<b>Nat-chan, 
Nat-chan,
 I baked some 
apple pie, 
have some</b>

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:46.060
<b>Hey, 
go somewhere
 else!!</b>

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:49.040
<b>Apple Pie</b>

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:08.590
<i>I'm quitting the team!</i>

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:12.270
Huh? Where's Ise?

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:15.370
Now that you mention it, he's not here.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.100
He was at school, right?

00:11:17.790 --> 00:11:21.490
Ise's finally started skipping, huh?

00:11:21.490 --> 00:11:23.070
Like hell he has!

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:26.540
Don't compare him to you shirkers!

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.560
Mutsumi-san.

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:39.300
Did Ise say anything to you?

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.800
No, nothing.

00:11:44.030 --> 00:11:46.460
Maybe he's not feeling well.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:50.950
He'll get better and
come back soon... probably.

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:12.360
Later.

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:15.550
Yeah, see you tomorrow.

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:19.740
<i>Natsuki, I'll come back tomorrow—</i>

00:12:42.610 --> 00:12:46.620
<b>Ise</b>

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:01.530
I'm home.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:04.020
You're late. What have you been doing?

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:06.010
I thought you quit the team.

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:11.110
Sorry. I stopped off somewhere.

00:13:13.740 --> 00:13:16.270
God, I feel like crap!

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:23.150
Go buy us something to eat.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.150
Summer Curry Fair

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:54.930
<i>They were all such great guys...</i>

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:59.860
<b>Summer Curry Fair</b>

00:14:12.170 --> 00:14:14.740
<i>Oh, right. Drinks.</i>

00:14:22.420 --> 00:14:23.580
Ha!

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:28.300
Running errands for your brother again?

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.900
Ebucchi...

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:32.850
Wait, what are you...

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:37.430
Oh, I was going to rent a DVD.

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:39.940
There's a place across the street
from your apartment.

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:42.170
I wanted to watch something dirty.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:45.070
In your school uniform?

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:47.750
Yeah. They turned me away.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:49.950
You really are brainless, aren't you?

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:55.330
Mutsumi-san was acting weird.

00:14:58.050 --> 00:15:00.270
Did your brother finally get pissed at you?

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:04.970
Yeah.

00:15:05.590 --> 00:15:10.230
Well, you've been avoiding it 
since you were in first year.

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:12.720
Must've been freaking terrifying.

00:15:13.420 --> 00:15:14.500
Hey, Ise.

00:15:14.500 --> 00:15:16.390
Shut up.

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:19.540
I'm quitting the team!

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:30.070
Your brother told you to 
go out and work, didn't he?

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:32.610
What?

00:15:32.610 --> 00:15:38.620
Is 100,000 yen enough for a week's pay?

00:15:40.190 --> 00:15:41.830
Y-Yeah...

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:45.790
Throw this in your brother's 
face and shut him up!

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:50.050
Where did you get this money?

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:52.220
Don't tell me you extorted first-years...

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:55.790
No, you idiot!

00:15:58.370 --> 00:16:00.060
You know how it is.

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:03.310
<b>Buy dinner
 for yourself</b>

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:03.310
<b>Mom</b>

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:08.830
Every day, they gave me more 
money than I could use.

00:16:08.460 --> 00:16:10.070
<b>Class
 Observation
 Notice</b>

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:27.090
B-But...

00:16:28.350 --> 00:16:34.090
All our third-years are 
great guys, aren't they?

00:16:36.530 --> 00:16:37.970
Hey!

00:16:38.310 --> 00:16:45.920
They recruited idiots like us and try 
desperately to stop us when we try to quit.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:47.620
<i>Seriously</i> desperately.

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:52.240
Did Mutsumi-san tell you?

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:55.870
He didn't have to tell me what was going on.

00:16:56.310 --> 00:16:59.220
Mutsumi-san's so easy to read.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:00.510
Oh...

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:21.010
<b>Rest In Peace</b>

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:57.930
My brother...

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:01.710
I don't blame him one bit.

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:09.190
I was supposed to go live 
with our uncle in Kyushu.

00:18:10.260 --> 00:18:11.860
But he...

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:14.190
I'm sorry.

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:17.610
I was ten when he was born.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:23.450
I was so happy about having 
a new family member...

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:29.210
Sending him to live with an unfamiliar family
at the same age is just too much.

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:32.370
I can't do that to him.

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:34.840
So...

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:38.270
So I'll take responsibility for him.

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:44.290
That's why he...

00:18:44.290 --> 00:18:45.970
I don't give a crap.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:51.170
He may have been a good brother to you 
back then, but what about now?

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:53.860
You wouldn't understand!

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:56.820
I don't want to.

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:06.010
Are you...

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:07.070
What?

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:09.250
Are you sure?

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:14.260
This three-year period is the 
only time we get to be in a club.

00:19:14.740 --> 00:19:16.710
We're not going to college.

00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:26.100
So let's see the second half through.

00:19:31.260 --> 00:19:38.520
Unlike us, Noka and Sumiyoshi will probably
go to college and keep playing rugby.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:40.110
Yeah, probably.

00:19:40.450 --> 00:19:43.870
But they don't even practice hard.

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:47.110
They've actually been 
trying lately, though.

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:49.210
Yeah,<i> lately</i>!

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:52.320
Besides, Ise!
You've got that guy to deal with!

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:53.000
What?

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:55.180
That little turd.

00:19:55.180 --> 00:19:56.920
Oh, right!

00:19:57.420 --> 00:20:01.050
I was trying to be a flanker first!

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:12.060
I hate watching Mutsumi-san and the other 
forwards in scrums from a distance.

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:15.050
I want to help out.

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:20.110
That's why I've been working out 
so I can switch to flanker!

00:20:20.600 --> 00:20:22.510
But that turd!

00:20:22.510 --> 00:20:24.380
Shut up! Keep it down!

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:28.430
And he's insolent towards his seniors, too.

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:30.360
I agree.

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:33.630
And it's only because
 all the second-years are like twigs

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:37.380
that Hyosu-san and Kasuga-san
became forwards.

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:42.540
You should work with the midget to 
send those two back to the backs.

00:20:42.540 --> 00:20:43.790
What?!

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:49.140
I guess you're right.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:51.850
We have to train the first-years, too.

00:20:51.850 --> 00:20:55.640
And if we don't get more forwards,
then next year...

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:57.480
Ha!

00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:00.860
You really should keep playing!

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:02.660
What's your problem?!

00:21:22.450 --> 00:21:24.850
That was a loan.

00:21:24.850 --> 00:21:26.470
You'd better pay me back someday!

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:32.100
After you throw it in
Haruki's face, of course!

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:35.850
Use honorifics when you're 
talking about my brother!

00:21:46.180 --> 00:21:47.480
You took your time.

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:49.000
Sorry.

00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:52.120
Who was that thug?

00:21:54.600 --> 00:21:57.550
I know he looks like a good-for-nothing, 
but he's still my teammate.

00:22:04.060 --> 00:22:09.190
If I hide my bags and take off my shirt,
maybe I can rent a DVD...

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:13.870
Nah, that'd never work.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
<b>Next Time: "You've Prepared"</b>

00:23:45.970 --> 00:23:49.140
Next time: "You've Prepared."
